WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.155 --> 00:00:00.992
- Wow!

00:00:00.992 --> 00:00:04.987
- ♫ Welcome home, family.

00:00:04.987 --> 00:00:06.995
Well, that was terrible.

00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:07.828
(grunting)

00:00:07.828 --> 00:00:08.661
- Ahhh!

00:00:11.436 --> 00:00:12.464
(swing music)

00:00:12.464 --> 00:00:13.432
- [Narrator] This week

00:00:13.432 --> 00:00:15.731
we are gonna be the perfect homemakers.

00:00:15.731 --> 00:00:18.021
- People talk about what an ideal time

00:00:18.021 --> 00:00:19.927
the mid-century was for families.

00:00:19.927 --> 00:00:21.652
This week, we're gonna give it a try

00:00:21.652 --> 00:00:23.438
and see if we can live up to that

00:00:23.438 --> 00:00:25.686
mid-century domestic ideal.

00:00:25.686 --> 00:00:27.172
- We have this handy chart that tells us

00:00:27.172 --> 00:00:31.717
what the perfect wife is and
we get to grade ourselves.

00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:32.702
How exciting.

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:34.480
- [Ochi] And scary.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.755
- Someone

00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:37.686
is gonna be negative.

00:00:37.686 --> 00:00:38.598
- Hey.

00:00:38.598 --> 00:00:41.098
(swing music)

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:48.728
- [Morgan] Puts her
cold feet on her husband

00:00:48.728 --> 00:00:50.456
at night to warm them.

00:00:50.456 --> 00:00:53.022
- A husband should be
there to warm you up.

00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:53.855
That's what I say.

00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:55.102
So negative one for me.

00:00:55.102 --> 00:00:58.030
- [Morgan] Religious,
sends children to church

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.489
or Sunday school and goes herself, well.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:01.393
- I could have had 10 points for this one.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:02.226
That sucks.

00:01:02.226 --> 00:01:03.515
- Has meals on time.

00:01:03.515 --> 00:01:04.967
(laughing) No.

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:07.759
- I can cook about two dinners.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:11.016
- Can carry on an
interesting conversation.

00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:13.408
I mean, I think I'm funny
and fascinating, so yeah.

00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:15.608
- Good sense of humor, jolly, and gay.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.441
Can't you tell?

00:01:16.441 --> 00:01:18.483
- Can play a musical instrument.

00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:20.506
Your wife is just there to entertain you

00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:22.503
with her interesting conversations

00:01:22.503 --> 00:01:24.302
and her violin playing.

00:01:24.302 --> 00:01:25.365
What the hell?

00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:26.575
- Dresses for breakfast.

00:01:26.575 --> 00:01:29.438
I don't eat breakfast
and I don't dress, so.

00:01:29.438 --> 00:01:31.855
- Man, it's not looking good.

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:36.880
- [Rose] I'm very poor,
parenthesis failure.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.577
I'm a failure as a wife
and a mother apparently.

00:01:39.577 --> 00:01:42.698
- As suspected I am a total failure.

00:01:42.698 --> 00:01:44.705
- That doesn't sound that great.

00:01:44.705 --> 00:01:47.193
But I heard that it's higher than Ochi.

00:01:47.193 --> 00:01:51.289
- When I looked at this, my
initial reaction was disgust.

00:01:51.289 --> 00:01:53.921
I would think that at the
time that my grandmother was

00:01:53.921 --> 00:01:55.857
this American housewife,

00:01:55.857 --> 00:01:58.905
she wanted to do these things.

00:01:58.905 --> 00:02:01.001
It just makes me angry to think that

00:02:01.001 --> 00:02:02.673
somebody could have looked at her

00:02:02.673 --> 00:02:04.865
and been checking off boxes.

00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:07.769
She handled her house and her life

00:02:07.769 --> 00:02:09.050
and her children with grace.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.097
I will be channeling
her and I also want to

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:16.570
pay a little homage to her
and all the parts she did.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.290
And see if I can do it too, right?

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.234
- After having my son, I got
to have year maternity leave.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:24.498
So, I got used to what it's
like to be a stay at home mom

00:02:24.498 --> 00:02:25.482
and I really loved it.

00:02:25.482 --> 00:02:27.866
So decided to quit my job
and not go back to work.

00:02:27.866 --> 00:02:30.330
You're always thinking
about am I doing it right?

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.986
I'm just nervous about these rules.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.202
About what my role's supposed to be.

00:02:35.202 --> 00:02:38.947
Hopefully it won't make me
unhappy with my choices.

00:02:38.947 --> 00:02:42.442
- My family dynamic has
been heavily shaped by

00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:45.250
my post-partum depression and OCD.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:48.298
So, my husband has been
running our household,

00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:51.450
as the primary caretaker for
going on seven years now.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.353
I have to live up to what he is already so

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:58.121
efficient at and what
he already does so well.

00:02:58.121 --> 00:03:00.089
It's kind of scary to
ask him to step aside

00:03:00.089 --> 00:03:02.154
and let me take the reigns of something

00:03:02.154 --> 00:03:05.369
that I have, quite honestly,
failed at in the past.

00:03:05.369 --> 00:03:07.441
Are you guys as stressed
out about this as I am?

00:03:07.441 --> 00:03:09.742
- I am so stressed about it.

00:03:09.742 --> 00:03:12.276
- I'm just nervous my husband's
going to get used to it.

00:03:12.276 --> 00:03:13.724
(laughing)

00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:17.917
- Supposed to dress myself
before I do anything else.

00:03:17.917 --> 00:03:20.308
I don't want to do it.

00:03:20.308 --> 00:03:22.361
- I'm wearing my grandma's apron now.

00:03:22.361 --> 00:03:24.442
I feel really hot in this things.

00:03:24.442 --> 00:03:27.371
Maybe it's oppression I feel.

00:03:27.371 --> 00:03:30.667
- I'm planning what
I'm gonna do this week.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:31.971
Here it is.

00:03:31.971 --> 00:03:34.987
Different church everyday
'cause that's the big points.

00:03:34.987 --> 00:03:38.654
- I don't think Rose
going to church counts.

00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:44.686
She walked in and then James
got bored and then she left.

00:03:44.686 --> 00:03:45.876
That doesn't count.

00:03:45.876 --> 00:03:47.515
- This morning I decided to get up

00:03:47.515 --> 00:03:51.083
and go balls to the wall put together

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:53.403
and care for my family at the same time.

00:03:53.403 --> 00:03:55.135
- [Ochi] Hey, guys, what are you doing?

00:03:55.135 --> 00:03:56.871
I was supposed to make you breakfast.

00:03:56.871 --> 00:03:58.311
- We were waiting for you for a while.

00:03:58.311 --> 00:04:01.359
- [Ochi] How can I get
ready and presentable?

00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:03.103
- You have to be presentable?

00:04:03.103 --> 00:04:05.061
- Check out my outfit.

00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:06.013
I think it's okay

00:04:06.013 --> 00:04:08.426
for what I'm trying to
accomplish this week.

00:04:08.426 --> 00:04:09.259
- I failed.

00:04:09.259 --> 00:04:10.251
I still have curlers in.

00:04:10.251 --> 00:04:11.323
My husband's gone to work

00:04:11.323 --> 00:04:13.420
and now my mom's here feeding
my daughter breakfast.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.753
- [Rose] Outsourcing the cleaning tasks.

00:04:18.473 --> 00:04:19.306
Thank you.

00:04:21.726 --> 00:04:23.656
- I went to get a glass for coffee

00:04:23.656 --> 00:04:27.178
and Scott has cleaned the kitchen.

00:04:27.178 --> 00:04:28.786
And ran the dishwasher.

00:04:28.786 --> 00:04:29.714
(laughing)

00:04:29.714 --> 00:04:31.427
- [Morgan Narrating] In a lot
of ways it was heartbreaking

00:04:31.427 --> 00:04:34.522
because it was a reminder
of how little faith

00:04:34.522 --> 00:04:37.028
he has in me as a homemaker

00:04:37.028 --> 00:04:39.180
and how truly earned

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:41.636
that lack of faith has been.

00:04:41.636 --> 00:04:43.476
- I can't do it, I'm too tired.

00:04:43.476 --> 00:04:45.004
This is so much effort.

00:04:45.004 --> 00:04:46.636
- This is not easy.

00:04:46.636 --> 00:04:48.436
- So stressed out right now.

00:04:48.436 --> 00:04:50.076
I had a last minute meeting.

00:04:50.076 --> 00:04:50.996
I have no food.

00:04:50.996 --> 00:04:52.468
I have nothing prepared.

00:04:52.468 --> 00:04:54.828
It said I had to have
meals delivered on time.

00:04:54.828 --> 00:04:57.071
It didn't say that they
had to be homemade.

00:04:57.071 --> 00:04:59.405
If those ladies had Postmates,

00:04:59.405 --> 00:05:00.924
they'd be using it.

00:05:00.924 --> 00:05:04.236
The more I tried to check
each box off on the guide.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.996
It was just one failure
after another after another.

00:05:06.996 --> 00:05:09.452
- So I was going to clean the kitchen,

00:05:09.452 --> 00:05:12.675
but I made these amazing pancakes.

00:05:12.675 --> 00:05:15.923
And Delilah asked me to sit
with her while she ate them.

00:05:15.923 --> 00:05:16.891
And you know what?

00:05:16.891 --> 00:05:18.976
It's a lot more fun.

00:05:18.976 --> 00:05:22.726
- [Ochi] What do you
want for breakfast, Pam.

00:05:23.964 --> 00:05:27.296
The one thing I know how to make.

00:05:27.296 --> 00:05:29.928
I think I would love to
keep cooking going forward.

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:31.005
- I was really surprised

00:05:31.005 --> 00:05:32.945
that I actually enjoyed cooking this week.

00:05:32.945 --> 00:05:34.393
Dinner is served.

00:05:34.393 --> 00:05:35.521
It looks okay.

00:05:35.521 --> 00:05:38.255
There was a really great
satisfaction in it.

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:40.598
- It was mainly the gratitude
on my family's face.

00:05:40.598 --> 00:05:43.993
I'm really happy that I
feel like doing it more for

00:05:43.993 --> 00:05:45.994
my own reasons for my family.

00:05:45.994 --> 00:05:48.466
But going forward, I'm
not gonna be cooking

00:05:48.466 --> 00:05:51.426
because that's what the
wife chart told me to do.

00:05:51.426 --> 00:05:54.832
- This scale has been
haunting me this whole week.

00:05:54.832 --> 00:05:58.727
It's been on my fridge and I
stare at it and I get angry.

00:05:58.727 --> 00:06:00.771
Goodbye, patriarchy.

00:06:00.771 --> 00:06:03.512
- I still sewed no
buttons, darned no socks.

00:06:03.512 --> 00:06:06.280
- Darn it, did not
accomplish this task again.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.536
- Neat house keeper.

00:06:07.536 --> 00:06:08.673
Mmmmmmmm.

00:06:08.673 --> 00:06:09.506
- Has meals on time?

00:06:09.506 --> 00:06:10.625
No, I did not do that one.

00:06:10.625 --> 00:06:11.985
No meals were on time.

00:06:11.985 --> 00:06:14.097
- I know they mean dresses
nice for breakfast,

00:06:14.097 --> 00:06:14.930
but I don't care.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.176
I had clothes on.

00:06:16.176 --> 00:06:18.093
- I think I did better.

00:06:19.484 --> 00:06:21.195
- [Rose] Wait, what?

00:06:21.195 --> 00:06:22.770
Wow, that's crazy.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.170
I must have cheated.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.067
- Woohoo! I'm average.

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.263
- I just got so excited that I raised up

00:06:28.263 --> 00:06:29.184
on this horrible scale.

00:06:29.184 --> 00:06:31.010
Then I realized I don't care.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.072
There's no such thing
as a perfect homemaker.

00:06:33.072 --> 00:06:33.905
Nor should there be.

00:06:33.905 --> 00:06:36.696
- The only perfect is
the best that you can be

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:39.136
for yourself and for your family.

00:06:39.136 --> 00:06:41.019
- It just made me really happy

00:06:41.019 --> 00:06:43.810
to be in such an equal
partnership with my husband.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.513
- When I looked at this
sheet, I was angry.

00:06:45.513 --> 00:06:47.634
And I thought women
shouldn't have to do this.

00:06:47.634 --> 00:06:48.737
This is bullshit.

00:06:48.737 --> 00:06:51.034
But as I went through the week, I realized

00:06:51.034 --> 00:06:55.460
that my own husband was
doing all of these things

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.661
and that's not right either.

00:06:57.661 --> 00:07:00.044
After this week, I'm committed to

00:07:00.044 --> 00:07:02.252
creating an equal partnership in the home.

00:07:02.252 --> 00:07:04.654
- Being a stay at home
mom has been my choice.

00:07:04.654 --> 00:07:07.205
Back then women didn't have a choice.

00:07:07.205 --> 00:07:10.045
- Maybe grandma had this idyllic life

00:07:10.045 --> 00:07:12.828
because that was the only option for her.

00:07:12.828 --> 00:07:15.348
Once it started getting into the 70s,

00:07:15.348 --> 00:07:17.740
she went back to school
and got her degree.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.749
Who knows what she would have
accomplished with her life

00:07:20.749 --> 00:07:22.925
if those opportunities had been there

00:07:22.925 --> 00:07:24.612
for her when she was younger.

00:07:24.612 --> 00:07:27.524
- No one should have to
devote their entire life

00:07:27.524 --> 00:07:30.509
to their family because
it is expected of them.

00:07:30.509 --> 00:07:31.806
- To me this is such a special role,

00:07:31.806 --> 00:07:34.404
but in the future hope
that people can enjoy it

00:07:34.404 --> 00:07:37.140
and not feel so many external pressures.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.700
- I don't think a woman can have it all.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:43.684
Having it all is trying to do everything

00:07:43.684 --> 00:07:47.540
that society tells you you should have.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:51.156
I believe that a woman can
have everything that she wants.

00:07:51.156 --> 00:07:52.993
So what's really important is knowing

00:07:52.993 --> 00:07:56.412
what you want for yourself
and for your family.

00:07:56.412 --> 00:07:59.079
(calming music)

